Superseding what I said above about keeping the `startsWith("[")` check. #19160 and #19173 have since merged, so `main` now carries two copies of this block, and both drop that check - #19366 made `ParseContext.host()` strip brackets, so `DbInfo.getServerAddress()` always holds the bare address and the guard can't fire. The merged copies also name the builder `poolName` rather than `result`. Worth matching them exactly so the later cleanup is trivial.

```suggestion
    StringBuilder poolName = new StringBuilder();
    if (serverAddress != null) {
      if (serverAddress.indexOf(':') >= 0) {
        poolName.append('[').append(serverAddress).append(']');
      } else {
        poolName.append(serverAddress);
      }
      if (serverPort != null) {
        poolName.append(':').append(serverPort);
      }
    }
    if (dbNamespace != null) {
      if (poolName.length() > 0) {
        poolName.append('/');
      }
      poolName.append(dbNamespace);
    }

    return poolName.length() == 0 ? DEFAULT_DATA_SOURCE_NAME : poolName.toString();
```

I opened #19370 to fold the copies into one shared helper.

